.SS "int32_t schultz_font_system_create (\fBschultz_font_system\fP ** out_system)"

.PP
Creates a font system and starts FreeType\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIout_system\fP Receives the new system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when out_system is NULL or FreeType refused to start, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void schultz_font_system_destroy (\fBschultz_font_system\fP * system)"

.PP
Destroys a font system, unloading every font it still holds\&. Every handle the system issued becomes stale\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The system to destroy\&. NULL is accepted and does nothing\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_load_file (\fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, const char * path, float size_px, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_font)"

.PP
Loads a font file at one pixel size\&. The file is read into memory and kept, so the file itself need not remain available afterwards\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The system to load into\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIpath\fP Path to a TrueType or OpenType file\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIsize_px\fP Pixel size to bind the face to\&. Must be greater than zero\&. 
.br
\fIout_font\fP Receives the font handle\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for a bad argument, SCHULTZ_ERR_UNREADABLE when the file is missing, unreadable, or holds no face FreeType can read, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_load_memory (\fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, const void * bytes, size_t length, float size_px, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_font)"

.PP
Loads a face from bytes already in memory\&. For a face that never was a file on this machine: one in a resource bundle, an Android asset, a zip, or one that arrived over the network\&. The bytes are copied, so the caller may free or reuse its buffer as soon as this returns\&.
.PP
Everything else works the same as a face loaded from a file, including asking for it again at another size\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system to load into\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIbytes\fP The face, in any format FreeType reads\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIlength\fP How many bytes\&. Must not be zero\&. 
.br
\fIsize_px\fP Pixel size to bind the face to\&. Must be above zero\&. 
.br
\fIout_font\fP Receives the font handle\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for a bad argument, SCHULTZ_ERR_UNREADABLE for bytes FreeType would not read, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_handle\fP schultz_font_builtin (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, uint32_t token)"

.PP
The face compiled into the library for one theme font slot\&. Schultz ships three DejaVu faces and one emoji face inside itself, so a program that says nothing about fonts still draws text\&. They are loaded when the font system is created and live as long as it does\&.
.PP
A host rarely needs this\&. A theme falls back to these on its own for any font slot nothing was put in, which is the point of them; this is here for a host that wants to name one directly\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system to ask\&. NULL yields SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE\&. 
.br
\fItoken\fP One of SCHULTZ_TOKEN_FONT_BODY, _TITLE, _MONO or _EMOJI\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The font, or SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE for a token that names no slot\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_unload (\fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font)"

.PP
Unloads a font and invalidates its handle\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The system holding the font\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP The font to unload\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the font is not loaded, which includes unloading twice\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_set_emoji (\fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font)"

.PP
Sets the face that draws emoji\&. No text face carries emoji, so a string holding one takes two faces to draw\&. Shaping splits the string where the chosen face stops having glyphs and gives those parts to this one; the split is made a character at a time as a person sees them, so a flag or a family stays one picture\&.
.PP
The system starts with the face compiled into the library, so this only needs calling by a host that wants its own artwork\&. The face is asked for at whatever size the text around it is set in, the same way any face is, so one call here covers every size\&.
.PP
This is the only face consulted when the chosen one comes up short, which makes it the answer for emoji and not for a missing script\&. Text in a script the body font does not cover needs a body font that does\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP The face to draw them with, or SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE for none, which leaves an emoji to draw as whatever the chosen face shows for a character it does not have\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when system is NULL, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the font is not loaded\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_handle\fP schultz_font_emoji (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system)"

.PP
Returns the face set by schultz_font_set_emoji\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system\&. NULL yields SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The face, or SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE when there is none\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_is_fixed_pitch (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font)"

.PP
Whether every glyph in a face is the same width\&. What makes a face a code face\&. The font says so in its own tables, so this is what the designer declared rather than a guess from measuring\&.
.PP
Asked when text has to be described to something outside the toolkit, such as a clipboard format that names a family rather than carrying the face\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP A handle from schultz_font_load_file or _load_memory\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Nonzero when the face is fixed pitch\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_is_bold (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font)"

.PP
Whether a face is the bold member of its family\&. The face says so in its own tables, so this is what the designer declared rather than a guess from measuring stem widths\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP A handle from schultz_font_load_file or _load_memory\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Nonzero when the face is bold\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_is_italic (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font)"

.PP
Whether a face is the slanted member of its family\&. True for an italic face and for an oblique one\&. The two are drawn differently, a true italic having letter shapes of its own rather than a sheared upright, but a face is one or the other and never both, so nothing that chooses a face has to tell them apart\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP A handle from schultz_font_load_file or _load_memory\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Nonzero when the face is italic or oblique\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_has_glyph (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font, uint32_t codepoint)"

.PP
Reports whether a face can draw a character\&. This asks the face's own character map, so it answers for the character rather than for how it would be shaped: a face may map every character of a sequence and still have no single picture for the sequence itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system holding the font\&. NULL yields zero\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP The face to ask\&. 
.br
\fIcodepoint\fP The Unicode character\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Nonzero when the face has a glyph for it\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_has_color_glyph (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font, uint32_t codepoint)"

.PP
Reports whether a face draws a character in colours of its own\&. The stronger question, and the one that decides which face draws what\&. A text face covers a surprising number of emoji as plain outlines, so asking only whether it has the character hands a smiling face to whichever face happens to be asked first and draws it as line art\&. Asking which face has the colours settles it\&.
.PP
It is also narrower than asking whether the face has colour at all: an emoji face carries the digits and the joiners too, for the sequences they take part in, and those are one colour like any letter\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The font system holding the font\&. NULL yields zero\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP The face to ask\&. 
.br
\fIcodepoint\fP The Unicode character\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Nonzero when the face draws it in colour\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_get_metrics (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font, \fBschultz_font_metrics\fP * out_metrics)"

.PP
Reads a font's vertical metrics\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The system holding the font\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP The font to query\&. 
.br
\fIout_metrics\fP Receives the metrics\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when out_metrics is NULL, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the font is not loaded\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "float schultz_font_size (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font)"

.PP
Returns the pixel size a font was loaded at\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The system holding the font\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP The font to query\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The pixel size, or 0\&.0 when the font is not loaded\&. 
