.SS "int32_t schultz_font_at_size (\fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font, float size_px, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_font)"

.PP
Returns the same face at another pixel size\&. A face is bound to one pixel size, because that is what FreeType and HarfBuzz both want, so a font handle names a face and a size together\&. Asking for another size gives back a handle already loaded at it when there is one, and loads it once otherwise\&. Sizes are compared after rounding to whole pixels, which is what FreeType is given\&.
.PP
This is what lets \fCfont\&.size\fP in a style mean anything, and what lets a page be rendered at print resolution with its glyphs rasterized at that resolution rather than scaled up from screen size\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The system holding the font\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP A font already loaded\&. 
.br
\fIsize_px\fP The pixel size wanted\&. Must be greater than zero\&. 
.br
\fIout_font\fP Receives the handle for that size\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the font is not loaded, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_font_at_style (\fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_handle\fP font, int32_t bold, int32_t italic, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_font)"

.PP
Returns another member of the same family, at the same size\&. The companion to schultz_font_at_size: that one keeps the face and changes the size, this one keeps the size and changes the face\&.
.PP
This is what makes a Bold button possible\&. A program cannot name the bold handle for whatever the caret is sitting in, because it does not know which face that is, and a selection may cover several\&. So it asks for bold and italic as a wish, and the family answers with a face\&.
.PP
Which family a face belongs to, and which member of it a face is, both come from the face's own tables\&. So faces group themselves as they are loaded and nothing has to be declared\&. The faces compiled into the library include the whole DejaVu Sans family, so bold and italic work with no setup\&.
.PP
Nothing is synthesized\&. When the family has no member with the styles asked for, the closest one it does have comes back, and a family with nothing closer answers with the face that was passed in\&. A face that names no family is always its own answer\&. So this call never fails for want of a face, and a caller can use what it returns without checking which it got\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The system holding the font\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP A font already loaded\&. 
.br
\fIbold\fP Nonzero for the bold member\&. 
.br
\fIitalic\fP Nonzero for the italic or oblique member\&. 
.br
\fIout_font\fP Receives the handle\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the font is not loaded, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint32_t schultz_font_count (const \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system)"

.PP
Counts loaded fonts\&. A new system is not empty\&. It loads every face compiled into the library, so a host that has loaded nothing still sees them here\&. That is one per theme font slot, plus the faces that complete a family without filling a slot\&. See schultz_font_builtin and schultz_font_at_style\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsystem\fP The system to query\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of fonts currently loaded\&. 
.RE
.PP

